1. CHECK WHETHER A STRING IS PALINDROME
==============================================================================

A palindrome reads the same from left to right and right to left.

Examples:

madam  -> Palindrome
level  -> Palindrome
java   -> Not Palindrome

CODE:

public static boolean isPalindrome(String str) {

    if (str == null) {
        return false;
    }

    int left = 0;
    int right = str.length() - 1;

    while (left < right) {

        if (str.charAt(left) != str.charAt(right)) {
            return false;
        }

        left++;
        right--;
    }

    return true;
}

INPUT:

System.out.println(isPalindrome("madam"));
System.out.println(isPalindrome("java"));

OUTPUT:

true
false

EXPLANATION:

Two pointers are used.

left starts from the beginning.
right starts from the end.

Characters are compared until both pointers meet.

TIME COMPLEXITY:

O(N)

SPACE COMPLEXITY:

O(1)

INTERVIEW ANSWER:

"I used two pointers to compare characters from both ends. If any characters
are different, the string is not a palindrome. The time complexity is O(N)
and no additional collection is required."

