public static boolean isRotation(String first, String second) {

    if (first == null || second == null) {
        return false;
    }

    return first.length() == second.length()
            && (first + first).contains(second);
}

INPUT:

System.out.println(isRotation("abcde", "cdeab"));

OUTPUT:

true

EXPLANATION:

first + first becomes:

abcdeabcde

This contains:

cdeab

The strings must have the same length.

TIME COMPLEXITY:

The conceptual interview answer is O(N), although the exact complexity of
contains() depends on the Java substring-search implementation.

