6. LONGEST VALID PARENTHESES
==============================================================================

INPUT:

String s = "(()";

EXPECTED OUTPUT:

2

CODE:

public static int longestValidParentheses(String s) {

    Deque<Integer> stack = new ArrayDeque<>();

    stack.push(-1);

    int maxLength = 0;

    for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {

        if (s.charAt(i) == '(') {

            stack.push(i);

        } else {

            stack.pop();

            if (stack.isEmpty()) {

                stack.push(i);

            } else {

                maxLength =
                    Math.max(maxLength, i - stack.peek());
            }
        }
    }

    return maxLength;
}

OUTPUT:

2

EXPLANATION:

The stack stores indexes rather than characters.

-1 acts as the initial boundary.

For '(':
    Store its index.

For ')':
    Remove the matching opening index.

If the stack becomes empty:
    Current closing bracket becomes the new invalid boundary.

Otherwise:

Current valid length = current index - top boundary index

TIME COMPLEXITY:

O(N)

SPACE COMPLEXITY:

O(N)

