27. FUTURE VS COMPLETABLEFUTURE
==============================================================================

FUTURE:

Future<String> future =
        executor.submit(() -> loadPayment());

String result = future.get();

get() normally blocks until the result becomes available.

COMPLETABLEFUTURE:

CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(
        this::loadPayment
)
.thenApply(this::validatePayment)
.thenAccept(this::savePayment)
.exceptionally(exception -> {

    log.error("Payment failed", exception);

    return null;
});

DIFFERENCE:

Future:
    Basic asynchronous result holder.
    Difficult to chain multiple operations.
    get() is blocking.

CompletableFuture:
    Supports chaining.
    Supports combining tasks.
    Supports callbacks.
    Supports exception handling.
    Can provide non-blocking completion stages.

