32. ARRAYLIST LOOP OUTPUT
==============================================================================

CODE:

List<Integer> list = new ArrayList<>();

list.add(1);

for (int i = 0; i < list.size(); i++) {

    list.add(2);

    System.out.println(list.get(i));
}

OUTPUT:

1
2
2
2
2
...

Eventually, the program can terminate with OutOfMemoryError.

WHY?

Initially:

i = 0
list.size() = 1

Every iteration:

i increases by 1.
list size also increases by 1.

Therefore:

i < list.size()

continues to remain true.

FIX:

int originalSize = list.size();

for (int i = 0; i < originalSize; i++) {

    list.add(2);

    System.out.println(list.get(i));
}

