==============================================================================
53. @Transactional PROPAGATION LEVELS
==============================================================================

REQUIRED:

Default.

Joins the existing transaction or creates a new one.

REQUIRES_NEW:

Suspends the current transaction and creates a new transaction.

SUPPORTS:

Uses the existing transaction if present. Otherwise runs without one.

MANDATORY:

Requires an existing transaction. Throws an exception if none exists.

NOT_SUPPORTED:

Suspends the current transaction and runs without a transaction.

NEVER:

Throws an exception if a transaction exists.

NESTED:

Creates a nested transaction using a savepoint when supported.

CODE:

@Transactional(
    propagation = Propagation.REQUIRES_NEW
)
public void saveAudit() {
}

USE CASE:

An audit record may need its own independent transaction.

Spring documents `@Transactional` as a way to declare transactional semantics
at method or class level. 【2-efdbd0】

IMPORTANT:

Transaction behavior is normally proxy-based.

Calling a transactional method from another method in the same class may
bypass the proxy.

