83. KUBERNETES FAILOVER
==============================================================================

CONTAINER FAILURE:

Kubelet can restart the container according to Pod restart policy.

POD FAILURE:

Deployment and ReplicaSet maintain the desired number of Pod replicas.

NODE FAILURE:

Pods managed by controllers can be replaced on available nodes after the
cluster detects the node condition and controller behavior applies.

READINESS PROBE:

readinessProbe:

  httpGet:
    path: /actuator/health/readiness
    port: 8080

  initialDelaySeconds: 20
  periodSeconds: 10

A failed readiness probe prevents the Pod from being considered ready for
normal Service traffic.

LIVENESS PROBE:

livenessProbe:

  httpGet:
    path: /actuator/health/liveness
    port: 8080

  initialDelaySeconds: 30
  periodSeconds: 10

A failed liveness probe can cause the container to be restarted.

HIGH AVAILABILITY CONTROLS:

1. Multiple replicas.
2. Readiness probe.
3. Liveness probe.
4. Pod anti-affinity or topology spreading where needed.
5. Pod Disruption Budget.
6. Multiple worker nodes.
7. Monitoring and alerting.

